LICENSE -- NOT YET CHOSEN.

This is a placeholder, not a license grant. No license terms apply to
this repository until this file is replaced with a real one.

This is a deliberate omission, not an oversight: this project may become
a commercial product, and the choice between something permissive
(MIT, Apache 2.0), something copyleft, or a proprietary/all-rights-reserved
license has real consequences for that -- for example, a permissive
license would let anyone freely reuse or fork the codebase, which may
conflict with commercial intent. That is a business decision for the
project owner to make explicitly, not one to default into silently.

Until this file is replaced: treat this repository as All Rights
Reserved by default -- the safe assumption when no license has been
chosen -- not as freely licensed for reuse.
